        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\"></td><td colspan=\"3\">Relevant credentials</td></tr><tr><td>Security appliances</td><td>Comment</td><td>EVCC (EV)</td><td>SECC (EVSE) private SECC (for PE only)</td><td>Secondary actor</td></tr><tr><td>Simplified certificate management in private environment -challenge 1 -manufacturer installs trust anchors Please refer to H.1.2</td><td>DC/AC charging with simplified key management -TLS authentication of SECC -TLS authentication of EVCC -TLS based confidential data exchange between EV and SECC (service discovery, power delivery, metering) -TLS based integrity of data between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering) TLS: AES used for stream/session encryption, ECDH used for key exchange</td><td>Vehicle leaf key pair (vehicle leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by an OEM root CA or a V2G root CA All vehicle sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the SECC leaf certificate PE private root CA certificate(s) installed by the OEM</td><td>PE TLS key pair (PE TLS private key and certificate) certified by PE private root CA All PE sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the PE certificate OEM root CA certificate(s) (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise) installed by the private SECC manufacturer</td><td>PE private root CA key pair</td></tr><tr><td>Simplified certificate management in private environment -challenge 2 -user installs trust anchors Please refer to H.1.2</td><td>DC/AC charging with simplified key management -TLS authentication of SECC -TLS authentication of EVCC -TLS based confidential data exchange between EV and SECC (service discovery, power delivery, metering) -TLS based integrity of data between EV and EVSE (service discovery, power delivery, metering) TLS: AES used for stream/session encryption, ECDH used for key exchange</td><td>Vehicle leaf key pair (vehicle leaf private key and certificate for TLS) certified by a sub-CA which was certified by an OEM root CA or a V2G root CA All vehicle sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the vehicle certificate OEM root CA certificate (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate otherwise) (installed by OEM to provide it to private SECC in CPM4PE) PE private root CA certificate(s) installed by the user</td><td>PE TLS key pair (PE TLS private key and certificate) certified by PE private root CA All PE sub-CA certificates of the certificate chain above the PE certificate PE private root CA certificate (installed by private SECC manufacturer to provide it to EV in CPM4PE) OEM root CA certificate(s) (if not below a V2G root. V2G root CA certificate(s) otherwise) installed by the user</td><td>PE private root CA key pair</td></tr></table>",
